            <ArticleTitle>Profit-driven drug testing.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>13-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3109/15360288.2011.650358</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Random drug testing of people being treated for chronic pain has become more common. Physicians may drug test patients on opioid therapy as a result of concerns over prosecution, drug misuse, addiction, and overdose. However, profit motive has remained unexplored. This article suggests profits also drive physician drug-testing behavior and evidence is offered, including an exploration of Medicare reimbursement incentives and kickbacks for drug testing.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
